ask: Fix two live bugs in build_obligation_pipeline.py (Imaan's AFS obligation pipeline) ahead of the client demo

Context:
This pipeline reads 10 topic JSONL files (BOL → OBL → Topic → AFS lineage), joins them per obligation (OBLIGOR_NUMBER + OBLIGATION_NUMBER), applies the Column C transforms and the 6 calculated business-rule fields, and writes two Bigtable tables: Table A (full) and Table B (essential). This is the version going to the client presentation.

Source of truth: The live lineage workbook, specifically:

Tab BOL>OBL>Topic->AFS
Tab Business Rules -Cal fields (rows 3–9 define the 6 calculated fields: CURR_PRIN_BAL_AMT, CURR_LINE_AMT, LOAN_LINE_TYPE, BALANCE, INTEREST_PAID_YTD, INT_PAYMENT_DATE)

No field or logic may be invented beyond what this sheet and the pipeline's own write-up (Obligation_pipeline_writeup.md, 9-item issue register) state. Any gap not sourced in the sheet must be left as an explicit off-by-default extension point, not guessed.

Bugs reported live (verbatim from the Imaan/Hemanth sync):

"Some of the loan line types come in as null."
"Some of the balance amounts are a little bit weird... not even sure if they should be negative."

Required fix — Bug 1 (null LOAN_LINE_TYPE):
Root cause: the join between account_relationships_accounts_supplementals, account-supplementals, and account-loanslinesleases-lcm (row 5 of the Business Rules tab, used in resolve_loan_line()'s takedown-chain walk) is an exact string match on OBLIGOR_NUMBER/OBLIGATION_NUMBER. The write-up's own ISSUE 3 flags that zero-padding format between topics is unconfirmed. A format mismatch (e.g. "10" vs "0000000010") causes a silent miss → null.
Fix required: try the exact key first (so clean/consistent data behaves identically), fall back to a zero-padding-normalized key only on a miss. Must not change output on any existing passing test scenario.

Required fix — Bug 2 (wonky BALANCE):
Root cause: when more than one candidate transaction or balance-header record exists for an obligation, the code picks "whichever one is first in the list Beam hands back" (posted_txn_recs[0], unsorted scan for BALH299/balanceCode=10) — not guaranteed stable between runs, per the write-up's own ISSUE 1 note. The BALANCE formula itself (rows 6–7 of the sheet) is correct and must not be changed.
Fix required: make the record selection deterministic — sort candidates by recorded timestamp / source sequence number and always pick the same one (most recent).

Also close, while in there (both already flagged as open issues in the write-up):

SEQUENCE_NUMBER (ISSUE 2) — currently never populated. Add a pipeline-local, parallel-safe default: the chosen transaction's 1-based rank among that obligation's own transactions, oldest-first. Do not read "max from destination table" — unsafe with parallel Dataflow workers.
productCode 15/16 exclusion (ISSUE 4, row 2 of the sheet) — stated as a business rule but not sourced to any field anywhere in the workbook (verified across all 5 tabs). Add a named constant/switch that is off by default, not a guessed field.

Explicitly out of scope — do not touch:

ISSUE 1: one-row-per-transaction redesign (needs a row-key design decision)
ISSUE 5/6/7/8: which process-type list is authoritative, INTEREST_PAID_YTD year filter, INT_PAYMENT_DATE format, differing null defaults across legacy interfaces — all business/data-owner questions

Acceptance criteria:
Re-run all 9 scenarios in the write-up's Section 8 test matrix (3 copies, 57 rows) — every documented expected value must still match exactly. Any new behavior may only trigger on cases the current test data doesn't cover (e.g., mismatched padding, multiple candidate records).

That's the full, self-contained version — everything needed to fix Imaan's pipeline with no other context required.
